Alkalinity Enhancement from Coastal Outfalls v1.0\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H4RJ0NBR1S0JKNR/prj_1H502CZZH1S0VMYW/pjd_1KN0CB1171S0JZ7Z/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"Project Design Document | 27 Mar 2026\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H4RJ0NBR1S0JKNR/prj_1H502CZZH1S0VMYW/pjd_1JXD1TNRV1S0P404/operations_and_monitoring_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"See report\"},{\"h\":\"/ghg-entry/rmv_1KJJH4G6A1S0NDQD?tab=calculation-view\",\"t\":\"See GHG entry →\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H4RJ0NBR1S0JKNR/prj_1H502CZZH1S0VMYW/pjd_1KN548ZF91S018E5/monitoring_and_operations_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H4RJ0NBR1S0JKNR/prj_1H502CZZH1S0VMYW/pjd_1KN0CB1171S0JZ7Z/pdd.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H4RJ0NBR1S0JKNR/prj_1H502CZZH1S0VMYW/pjd_1KN0C9BFJ1S0ZACA/ghg_statement_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H4RJ0NBR1S0JKNR/prj_1H502CZZH1S0VMYW/pjd_1KN0C07391S0R0N0/verification_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"},{\"h\":\"https://storage.googleapis.com/isometric--production--eu--public-documents/spl_1H4RJ0NBR1S0JKNR/prj_1H502CZZH1S0VMYW/pjd_1KCPS2BK11S0T23J/monitoring_and_operations_report.pdf\",\"t\":\"PDF | ->\"}],\"text\":\"VALIDATED\\nMARINE\\n1,000Y+\\nNova Scotia Mineral OAE Project\\nPlanetary\\nISSUED\\n4,853.6\\nBUFFER POOL\\n97.075\\nCREDITING PERIOD\\n01 Feb 2024 to 31 Jan 2029\\nSummary\\nRemoval method\\nMonitoring locations\\nCalculation overview\\nProject documentation\\nCertificates\\nReversal risk\\nSummary\\n\\nPlanetary Technologies add alkaline compounds to seawater to enhance the natural ability of seawater to absorb atmospheric carbon dioxide, storing the carbon in dissolved carbon-containing ions in the oceans for 10,000-100,000 years.\\n\\nPROJECT DETAILS\\nCurrent verifier\\n350Solutions\\n->\\nProject code\\nF5X7\\nApproval date\\n31 Mar 2025\\nCurrent protocol version\\nOcean Alkalinity Enhancement from Coastal Outfalls v1.0\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nNova Scotia Mineral OAE Project\\nHow carbon is being removed\\n\\nMarine carbon dioxide removal (mCDR) leverages the ocean's natural capacity to absorb and store carbon for thousands of years. These pathways use the biogeochemical and physical properties of the ocean and other bodies of water to capture carbon dioxide from the atmosphere or to permanently store carbon already contained within them. Approaches to mCDR include Ocean Alkalinity Enhancement and Direct Ocean Capture and Storage.\\n\\nProject Design Document\\n27 Mar 2026\\nMonitoring locations\\n\\nOngoing monitoring is required in the outfall prior to discharge and at the edge of the mixing zone. These measurements are used for ensuring compliance with regulatory limits and Planetary’s self-imposed stop-trigger limits in their adaptive management plan. Stop-triggers include thresholds for avoiding alkalinity losses through secondary precipitation and biotic calcification, as well as environmental safety thresholds. See the Operations Report for more detail.\\n\\nSee report\\nCalculation overview\\nCalculations demonstrating 536.46 tCO₂e removed from Nova Scotia Mineral OAE Project on 15 Mar 2026\\nSee GHG entry →\\nNet CO₂e Removed\\n536.458 tCO₂e\\nSequestrations\\n642.394 tCO₂e\\n-\\nActivities\\n0\\n+\\nUncertainty Discount\\n105.935 tCO₂e\\n⌘ + scroll to zoom\\nView full screen\\nProject documentation\\nSubmission date\\tTitle\\tDownload\\n31 Mar 2026\\tMonitoring and Operations Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n27 Mar 2026\\tPDD\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n27 Mar 2026\\tGHG Statement Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n27 Mar 2026\\tVerification Report\\tPDF\\n->\\n\\n12 Dec 2025\\tMonitoring and Operations Report\\tPDF\\n->\\nShowing 5 of 16\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nCertificates\\nIssued\\n4,853.6\\nRetired\\n2,059\\nBuffer pool\\n97.075\\nCrediting period\\n01 Feb 2024 to 31 Jan 2029\\nIssuances\\nRetirements\\nIssue date\\tIssued\\tBuffer pool\\tSupplier allocation\\n30 Mar 2026\\t1,530.33\\t30.609\\t1,499.721\\n12 Dec 2025\\t1,507.98\\t30.16\\t1,477.82\\n01 Oct 2025\\t1,189.65\\t23.793\\t1,165.857\\n16 Jun 2025\\t625.64\\t12.513\\t613.127\\nShowing 4 of 4\\nPrevious\\nNext\\nReversal risk\\n\\nThe risk of reversal for this project has been assessed as very low. This means that 2% of certificates issued for this project are allocated to Planetary's buffer pool.\\n\\nTo date, this project has contributed 97.075 certificates to the buffer pool which holds a total of 97.075 certificates.\\n\\nPlanetary has no reversals to date.\\n\\nLearn more about reversal risk\"}"